#require "storage.eflint".

// no need to specify a context-expression, 
// a rich context is implicitly present as the knowledge base active when an expression is evaluated
Act read    Related to resource
Act write   Related to resource
Act create  Related to resource  
  Holds when True // all know resources can be created, unless further constraint 
  Creates owner-of(resource, actor) When Enabled(create()) // only 'new' resources can be created
  Conditioned by !(Exists owner-of: owner-of.resource == resource)
Act delete  Related to resource
Act compute Related to input, output
Placeholder input For resource
Placeholder output For resource

// make permissions explicit
// (a) permissions can be queried with `?--permission`
// or alternatively: `?--read`, `?--write`, `?--compute`
// can be used by the policy contract to pro-actively update the ledger when attributes change
Fact action Identified by READ, WRITE, CREATE, DELETE
Fact permission Identified by actor * action * resource
  Derived from permission(action = READ) When Enabled(read())
              ,permission(action = WRITE) When Enabled(write())
// (b) permissions can be queried with `?Enabled(read(actor, resource))`
// can be used by the PDP to ask the policy contract whether a request is permitted 

// (1) owners can read, write (and compute), and delete their resources
Extend Act read Holds when owner-of(owner=actor)
Extend Act write Holds when owner-of(owner=actor)
Extend Act compute Holds when owner-of(owner=actor, resource = input) 
                           && owner-of(owner=actor, resource = output)
Extend Act delete Holds when owner-of(owner=actor)
Extend Act create Holds when True // no constraints on creation (yet)

